// Topic: pattern. Language: en. The German version sits in pattern.de.gift.
//
// This file carries no YAML header. A header ahead of the first line becomes a
// question on import. The exception to format rule 3 and its reason stand in
// en.md, section 5. These six lines carry what the header would have carried.
//
// One example per question type. What does not stand here is not used.
// Every question carries its model answer and one sentence on why the correct
// answer is correct. That sentence stands as general feedback behind ####.
// No standard wording, neither in a question nor in an answer option.

$CATEGORY: pattern

// 1. Description. No question, no marks, only a text before a group.
// Recognisable by no brace following it.

::Note before the questions that follow::
The questions that follow test whether a requirement can be assigned to an
activity. References are by standard, clause and edition.

// 2. True or false.

::The order of assessment and selection::
The controls are determined from the risk treatment, and the comparison against
the annex comes after that.{TRUE
####Correct. ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 requires that order in 6.1.3, and the
comparison is a check for what was forgotten there and not a starting point.}

// 3. Multiple choice with one correct answer.

::The clause responsible for the scope::
In which clause of ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 is the scope of the ISMS required?{
=4.3 #Correct.
~6.1.3 #That is where the risk treatment stands.
~9.2 #That is where the internal audit stands.
~7.5 #That is where documented information stands.
####The scope is the first decision of the management system and therefore
stands in the clause about the context and not with the planning.}

// 4. Multiple choice with several correct answers. The weights on the correct
// ones add up to a hundred, a wrong one takes the whole mark off.

::What makes an internal audit::
Which two properties make a check an internal audit under
ISO/IEC 27001\:2022, 9.2?{
~%50%It is planned and follows a programme. #Correct.
~%50%It is carried out by somebody who is not responsible for the area
checked. #Correct.
~%-100%It is carried out by a certification body. #That would be a
certification audit and none of your own organisation.
~%-100%It happens without notice. #Notice is neither required nor forbidden.
####Planned and independent are the two properties without which a check is
only a look through.}

// 5. Short answer. Several spellings are recorded as correct.

::What is left after the treatment::
What is the name for what is left of a risk after the controls work?{
=residual risk
=the residual risk
####It is never zero. Anyone who takes it for zero has overestimated the
controls or not understood the risk, and it is expressly approved.}

// 6. Matching. There is no feedback per subquestion here, so the general
// feedback carries the reasoning for all pairs.

::Clause and activity::
Assign to each activity the clause of ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 that requires it.{
=Internal audit -> 9.2
=Management review -> 9.3
=Documented information -> 7.5
=Corrective action -> 10.2
####All four stand in the later part of the standard, because they concern the
operation and the improvement and not the build.}

// 7. Missing word. The choice stands in the middle of the sentence.

::Missing word, the clause for the internal audit::
The internal audit is required in {=9.2 ~9.1 ~9.3 ~10.1} of
ISO/IEC 27001\:2022.{####9.1 is the measurement, 9.3 the management review and
10.1 the improvement. The audit stands between them, because its result goes
into 9.3.}

// 8. Numerical question. The number after the colon is the tolerance.

::The number of clauses carrying requirements::
How many clauses of ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 carry requirements that are certified
against?{#7:0
####They are clauses 4 to 10. The clauses before them carry the scope of the
document, the references and the terms and are not audited.}

// 9. Essay. There is no automatic marking, so the general feedback carries the
// model answer that is marked against by hand.

::Reasoning for a control that is not applied::
An organisation does not apply a control from the annex. Write in two sentences
what has to stand in the statement of applicability about it.{
####Model answer. It has to say that the control is not applied and why not,
and the reasoning has to point back at the risk treatment. A pointer to the
control being expensive is no reasoning as long as no risk is named beside it.}
